From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:11:35 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Plutonium: Pluto Vim in the composer, and Hydra from
 the keyboard

The composer declares what it can do to Plutonium's vim mode
(PLUTO_VIM.md, "Pages that integrate"): submit, the prompt history, the
open / or @ menu (Ctrl+N, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+Y and Ctrl+E, yielded while it's
open, since Ctrl+N is a new thread), and the model and stash commands.
Each action runs the composer's own key handling.

It also fills the keys HYDRA_KEYBOARD.md gives pages (plutonium/
hydraKeys.ts): Space and Backspace page the timeline, Tab goes back
through recently used threads and H/L through the sidebar's, the g places
(gt the terminal, gb/gB the browser, ga an app, gf files, gd the diff, gs
the sidebar, gm the latest message, gp a waiting approval, gx what's under
the cursor) and the z shows (zt, zb, zs, zf, zd, zm). S labels what's on
screen and gw every word (plutonium/hints.ts). Outside insert mode the
editor yields Space, Backspace and Tab, which ProseMirror would take
first. The same keys work when the keyboard is on something that isn't a
field; y and n answer an approval gp went to. T3's commands run by name
through useChatShortcuts (plutonium:command), else as their keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
